            <ArticleTitle>[Analysis of the work of an analgesia service in an outpatient clinic].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>72-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The management of patients with chronic pain syndrome in out-patient clinics is a new form of specialized therapy. 347 cancer patients were treated using a modified &quot;analgetic staircase&quot; technique (14% of them at home), with an analgetic effect achieved in 60-70% of cases. The patients with pain syndrome were managed using sacral, epidural and subarachnoidal neurolysis blockades.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
